WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:01.934
-I always like seeing you.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:02.667
Thank you so much
for coming back

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:05.000
and coming to visit me.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.501
You want to sit on the couch?

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:07.601
-I'll do anything you say.

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:08.667
-No, no, no, no, no!

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:09.968
[ Laughter ]
You keep looking at it.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:12.100
But, yeah, you can lay down.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.767
[ Laughter ]
Sure, of course, yeah.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.267
Let's talk
about your life, yeah.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.434
Let's talk about your career.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:21.934
F. Murray Abraham,
you've had a fantastic career.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.300
-Yes.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.601
[ Laughter ]
Yes, I have, I have.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:26.601
It's been fanta--

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:28.367
Where is everybody?
-We're here.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.734
We're at "The Tonight Show."
Okay, perfect.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.968
I wanted to ask you a quick
question because I heard this

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:34.601
and tell me
if it's true or false.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.567
Not about "White Lotus,"
about you.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:37.934
Is that you got your start,

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.734
or one of your breaks,
being a Santa for Macy's.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:43.067
-Yeah, I was, yeah.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.300
I took it very seriously, too.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.400
-No, no, I really did.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.801
It was the one that was
in Queens at the time

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:53.400
and there were a lot of like

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.901
immigrants that were living
in Queens at the time.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:01:00.534
Very diverse.
And I used to ask, quietly,

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:03.901
the parents of the kids
what language they spoke

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.133
and then I would write out

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.300
how to say Merry Christmas
in their language.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.901
So, when the kid sat on my lap,

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.767
I'd say Merry Christmas
in that language

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:13.000
because it was --
and the kid would go --

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.367
[ Laughter ]
"It's Santa Claus!"

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:15.934
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:18.434
-Oh, boy, that's a great story.
-Yeah, it's true.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:21.634
That was really --
I was really serious

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:22.934
about it.
-That's a great -- I mean,

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:24.667
of all your acting roles,
that's one of --

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.067
that's probably one
of your best that you've got,

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.801
Santa Claus
in different languages.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:29.167
You know, I want to say
congratulations.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.734
You were nominated for an Emmy
for your voiceover work

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.968
[ Cheering and applause ]
in Marvel's --

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:36.300
in "Moon Knight,"
playing this character.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.934
That is you.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.901
That is what -- Yeah.
You're the voice of

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:41.801
Khonshu.
-Khonshu.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.100
-Khonshu.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.767
Is this a whole new fan base
for F. Murray Abraham?

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:48.934
-It's funny,
I get fan mail from China.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.801
-Oh, is that right?
-For this voice. I really do.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.968
I was going to have lunch
at a hangout of mine

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:57.334
in the Village and it was closed

00:01:57.334 --> 00:02:01.133
because there was a film,
a student film was being made.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.167
It's in the Village, near NYU.

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:05.567
And I'm looking like
in the window

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.200
and one of the kids,

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.968
young people
who's making the film, says,

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.000
"Are you in this movie?!"

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.868
And I looked at him
and someone else came over

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:15.667
and says,
"Do you know who this is?!

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.367
This is the voice of Khonshu!"

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.734
-Wow!
-I swear. That's the truth.

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.534
-Out of all your years
of acting...

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.834
-Yeah.
-...you've won an Academy Award.

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.367
-It's alright. I'll take it
where I can get it.

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:29.334
-Yeah, come on.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:31.100
Can we talk about "White Lotus"?

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.868
-Oh, yeah.
-We have to. You're fantastic.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.367
The finale aired
this past Sunday.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:37.167
No spoilers. Got giant ratings.
Everyone's talking about it.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.267
I don't want to give
too much away.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:40.634
But what did you think
of the finale,

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:42.901
can you say that?
-Oh. Oh.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.467
You got to -- You got to see it.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:46.834
For those of you who haven't
seen it, you're in for a shock.

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.167
It was some surprise.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.801
-Were you surprised, though?
-Yeah!

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.334
I decided not to see
anything until --

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.801
until the last segment
and I saw it this Sunday.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.734
I was really blown away.
I'm not going to say anything

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:57.834
about it because
you'll be surprised.

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.133
But I got to tell you
this, man --

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.067
it was the best experience
of my life.

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:03.300
You got to go to Sicily.
I mean, you really do.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.467
-I mean, it's beautiful.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:06.734
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:08.634
-We're not giving away
any trips to Sicily.

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.901
What more do you want?!
Gosh!

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:15.234
Give you cars, sweaters,
Janet Jackson tickets.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.901
[ Laughter ]
I mean, come on.

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:19.167
But you go there and Mike White.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.534
I know he's a genius,
but is he a genius?

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.968
-Absolutely, man.
-He is, right?

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.601
He's unbelievably genius.
-I mean, how many people

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:26.300
do you work for that you want
to work for again

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.701
and again and again?
-Yeah.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.634
-Am I right? Am I right?
-And you'd do anything for.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:30.834
-You're working for him, right?

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.267
-Why are you looking
at the band?

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.067
Everyone's very happy here,
yeah.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.367
[ Laughter ]
But you get offered the role

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:39.133
and it's just because they go,
"Hey, we want Murray Abraham.

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:40.267
-Oh.
He's the best."

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.200
-You read the script
and you want to do this.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.567
Are you kidding? I got lines
in there that are deathless.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:46.934
I got lines that I said
in that thing

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:48.801
that people were saying to me
on the street.

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.567
-Yeah. What is your
favorite line?

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:53.701
-Oh, my favorite line was
we were talking about the --

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:55.667
the aesthetics of a penis.

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.534
[ Laughter ]
Like -- Yeah, it was like,

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:58.868
"Is it beautiful?
Is it --"

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.567
And I said, "Well, it's a penis.

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:01.801
It's not a sunset."

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:05.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:07.067
I mean, that's a great line.
-That's a good line.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:08.901
That's a good line.
"It's not a sunset."

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:11.968
-And people in New York, I mean,
I don't know what --

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.467
They'll say,
"Hey, penis! Hey!"

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:17.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.601
-I get the same thing.

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:20.000
I get the same exact thing.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:25.000
-That's funny.
-How did they describe

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.167
the character to you when you --
-Oh, no, no.

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.400
You know,
you just give me the script

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.300
and you go,
"I got to do this, man."

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.100
-You just have to.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.167
-No, no, you got to do this.

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.300
-Because he's
a little problematic,

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.267
but you make him funny
and charming.

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:38.167
-Yeah, well, they're like people
I grew up with.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:39.400
-They are, yeah.
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.300
I'm first-generation American.
-Oh, wow.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.367
-I mean, these people.
I'm half Italian, half Syrian,

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:44.934
[ Cheering and applause ]
and these people were like that,
you know?

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:46.567
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:50.167
And you and Michael Imperioli
got together.

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:51.634
You felt like father
and son to me.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:53.067
-Well, I got to tell him, man,

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:54.801
Michael and I became
very good friends.

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:56.267
-Yeah?
-Yeah. It's lucky
when that happens.

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:57.901
Doesn't happen too often,
you know?

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.067
He's a good guy.
-Yeah.

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:01.234
-You just got nominated
for a Golden Globe

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.234
for your performance...

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.834
-Oh.
-...so, congratulations on that.

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:07.434
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:09.167
[ Rimshot ]
Awww!

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.734
Yeah. Oh, my God!

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:15.901
Oh, my God!

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:17.267
Are you --
Do you get excited about that?

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:18.934
You get a Golden Globe?
-Well, I already have one.

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:19.868
[ Laughter ]
-So you go -- Yeah.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:22.801
-[ Snaps fingers ]
-Wow! Wow!

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:24.534
Put it next to your Oscar.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:28.701
I'd like another Golden Globe.
-Ooh, yeah! Can we get him two?

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:30.467
Let's get him another
Golden Globe, come on.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:31.567
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.767
It's well-deserved.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:35.601
-And I'd like another Oscar.
-Yeah, you go.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.534
[ Laughter ]
-Hey, while we're at it.

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:37.667
While we're at it, why not?

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:39.400
Everyone wins.
I want to show a clip.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.501
Here's F. Murray Abraham
in "The White Lotus."

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:42.701
Take a look at this.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.267
-They probably don't want
to be escorts.

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:48.801
They're just poor and victims
of a [bleep] system.

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:51.367
-Women aren't all saints, Albie.

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:52.767
They're just like us.

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:55.834
-Have a good lunch.
[ Scoffs ]

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:56.534
[ Chair scrapes floor ]

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:57.334
-Where are you going?

00:06:00.901 --> 00:06:02.701
-Dad, what is the matter
with you?

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:05.534
I-I mean, you almost just --

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:06.534
-Just what?

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:08.067
-You know what.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.667
I'm trying to smooth things over
with Albie and with everyone

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:13.467
and that would -- you know,
that would really not be good.

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:15.534
-I can't be responsible
for everything I say.

00:06:15.534 --> 00:06:17.067
I'm concussed.

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:18.868
I just hit my head.
-Yeah.

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:20.033
[ Cheering and applause ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:21.033
"I can't be respons--

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:22.834
Hey, I'm concussed."
-Thank you, man.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:26.033
F. Murray Abraham, everybody.
-Thank you very much.

00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:28.934
-"The White Lotus" is available
now on HBO and HBO Max.

00:06:28.934 --> 00:06:31.300
More "Tonight Show"
after the break. Stick around.
-Thank you.

